crabbucket
==========

crabbucket is a static site framework in Rust, for landing pages and
documentation sites -- the kind that live next to a repository and get
deployed to GitHub Pages.

Its thesis is that a site is a typed value.  Links, frontmatter, design
tokens and the base path are all typed, so the failures that usually
break a small site -- a dead link, a page with no title, a renamed
colour, a stylesheet 404ing because the site is served from /repo/ --
are compile errors rather than production surprises.

  The build either fails, or the site is correct.

See the file doc/DESIGN for the full concept and the reasoning behind
each choice.  It is short, and it is meant to be argued with.

This is free software.  See the file COPYING for copying conditions.

  Copyright (C) 2026 Oddur Sigurdsson

