Status
------

Early.  The design is settled; the implementation is not.  Nothing here
is stable, including the parts that look stable.


At a glance
-----------

  Content     Markdown with `+++' TOML frontmatter, deserialized into
              your own structs.  Writing a page needs no Rust.  Headings
              are linkable and code is highlighted at build time.
  Links       Every internal link -- route, asset and heading fragment
              alike -- is resolved after rendering.  A dead one fails the
              build; there is no flag to turn it off.
  Components  maud functions.  Typed props, compile-checked HTML, no
              template language and no runtime.
  Design      One tokens file generates both Rust constants and CSS
              custom properties, so the two cannot drift apart.  Styles
              live beside their components and are namespaced.  A design
              system is a crate you depend on.
  Layouts     An associated type on the theme, so a layout that does
              not exist fails the build listing the ones that do.
  Client      Zero JavaScript by default.  Opt in to a 2.9KB gzipped
              router -- navigation, prefetching, copy buttons -- and to
              search.  Each ships nothing when it is not asked for.
  Dev loop    turborust.  crabbucket ships no dev server of its own.


Layout
------

  crates/crabbucket      the framework
  crates/crabbucket-cli  the `crab' executable
  crates/crabbucket-ui   the default design system and component kit
  examples/site          crabbucket's own site, built with crabbucket
  design/tokens.toml     the token source of truth
  doc/DESIGN             the concept
  cairn/items            the roadmap and the issues, one file each


Starting a site
---------------

  crab new my-project --router
  cd my-project
  crab build

That scaffolds a site that builds with no edits, including a
turborust.toml and a GitHub Pages workflow.


Building
--------

Rust 1.85 or newer is required.

  cargo build --release

A Makefile is provided for the usual GNU targets, so the following also
works and honours the customary `prefix' and `DESTDIR' variables:

  make
  make check
  make install prefix=/usr/local


Developing
----------

  turborust up

turborust rebuilds the example site when anything it depends on changes,
serves it with live reload, and shows build errors in a browser overlay.
See <https://github.com/oddurs/turborust>.


Reporting bugs
--------------

Please report bugs at <https://github.com/oddurs/crabbucket/issues>.


Files
-----

  AUTHORS      who wrote crabbucket
  COPYING      the GNU General Public License, version 3
  ChangeLog    a log of changes, newest first
  HACKING      notes for people working on the source
  NEWS         user-visible changes, newest first
  ROADMAP.md   what is planned, generated from cairn/items
  THANKS       people who have helped
  doc/DESIGN   the design, and the reasoning behind it
  doc/STABILITY what 1.0 promises, and what it does not
  doc/crab.1   the man page
